# UI & shadcn Standards

## Component Priority

1. Use installed shadcn primitives from `@/components/ui/*` first.
2. Never hand-roll buttons, inputs, cards, or progress bars when a shadcn component exists.
3. Wrap or extend in `components/` — do not edit `components/ui/*` unless fixing a bug.

Installed primitives: `Button`, `Card`, `Textarea`, `Badge`, `Progress`, `Separator`, `Tooltip`.

## Styling

- Tailwind utilities + CSS tokens from `app/globals.css` (`--primary`, `--background`, `--border`, etc.).
- Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for conditional classes.
- Prefer `variant` / `size` props over custom CSS.

## UX

- **Dark-first:** default dark theme; every component must work in light mode too.
- **RTL:** code blocks always `dir="ltr"`; UI text follows `isRTL`; Arabic font on container only.
- **Motion:** Framer Motion for meaningful transitions only (fade-in, progress fill, collapse) — no decorative noise.
- **Accessibility:** preserve focus rings, `aria-*`, and keyboard navigation from shadcn/Radix.

## Complexity

- Extract subcomponents when a file exceeds ~150 lines.
- No premature abstractions or unnecessary wrappers.
